This repository started from the TrustFake training framework distributed to
participants of the TReC 2026 research camp (TRAIL / Trust Valley), Project 02,
by Nicolas Sournac. That framework was imported unchanged in the first commit
(014053d, 2026-08-25) and is published here with the rest of the code under the
Apache License 2.0, as part of an open-source research programme. The parts
authored on top of it — the attack taxonomy and confidence axis, the
shard-disjoint split protocol, selective-classification, calibration and
moderation metrics, corruptions, the sweep and baseline tooling, Track B and
Track C, and the test suite — are by Samuel Renteria.

Datasets are downloaded by the user and never redistributed here:
  SID-Set  (huggingface.co/datasets/saberzl/SID_Set)   CC BY 4.0
  FakeClue (huggingface.co/datasets/lingcco/FakeClue)  Apache-2.0
Pretrained weights are fetched at run time from their own distributions
(torchvision, open_clip, Depth Anything V2 via transformers, fra31/auto-attack)
under their respective licenses.
